  "worked_solution": "We have $\\frac{2}{5}$ on the left and $\\frac{2}{10}$ on the right.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130082/assets/849573cc74dfd2c51479ae3c9c13e8993cfa7cf433887198abda16fe34704eb7.png)\n\nThe shape on the right-hand side is split into $2$ equal parts by a horizontal line. So, the shaded part on the left is $2$ times larger than the shaded part on the right. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{5}\\times \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{2}{10}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $2.$",
